        </p>
        <ul class="bullet-feature-list">
          <li><strong>The Contributory Framework (NPS):</strong> State employees joining regular service after September 1, 2005 are enrolled under the National Pension System (NPS), contributing 10% of their Basic Pay &plus; DA, with matching state contributions. Employee unions continue to campaign for the restoration of the defined-benefit <strong>Old Pension Scheme (OPS)</strong> or the state adoption of the <strong>Unified Pension Scheme (UPS)</strong> model.</li>
          <li><strong>Revision for Existing Pensioners:</strong> Over four lakh retired state employees and family pensioners will see their baseline monthly pension multiplied directly by the finalized fitment factor. The statutory minimum pension in Bihar will rise from ₹9,000 to approximately <strong>₹20,520 per month</strong> under the 2.28 factor.</li>
